  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 1239 AM MDT Tue Oct 27 2026\n\nWarm and dry through most of the week. Temperatures will be 5-10 \ndegrees above average around midweek, cooling a bit on Thursday \nafter a passing wave shoves a dry cold front through the plains. \n\nLong-range forecast remains consistent with recent model runs, \nthough some of the fine details are still unclear. A broad upper \ntrough will amplify over the Pacific Northwest, moving down the \ncoast and tracking east through the weekend. Southwest flow will \nsettle over our area out ahead of the system, with a renewed \nmoisture tap leading to accumulating mountain snow starting on \nFriday. Beyond that, latest guidance has a low pressure system \nmoving into our area later in the weekend, hinting at cooler and \nmore unsettled weather into early next week. However, model \nsolutions greatly diverge on the path and evolution of this system, \nso it will likely be several days before those details become \ncertain.",
